  "body": "Add a user guide showing how to drive SolidCraft and CamCraft together in one AI conversation.\n\n## Scope\n- Add a guide under `docs/user-guide/` explaining how to connect one external MCP agent (Claude Code, Codex CLI, or Gemini/Antigravity CLI) to both `solidcraft-cli mcp --connect` and `camcraft-cli mcp --connect` today.\n- Walk through one end-to-end example: create a simple part in SolidCraft, save `.sc` (or export `.step`), import and link it in CamCraft (`import_model`, `LinkWatch`), detect features (`detect_holes` / `detect_pockets`), generate, and verify.\n- Document the cross-app safety boundaries: two separate undo stacks, manual confirmation for posting and machine edits, and cloud privacy rules for CAD parameters and screenshots.\n- Use only live MCP tool names from `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs` and public SolidCraft CLI documentation.\n\nDone means: The guide exists under `docs/user-guide/`, every CamCraft MCP tool name matches `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`, and the guide documents both live `.sc` linking and the cross-app undo and privacy rules.\n\nPart of #3793\n",
